# Mimic Masters Website

Official website for **Mimic Masters**, hosted on GitHub Pages.

Live site: https://alviespurlock.github.io/MimicMastersWebsite/

## Pages (22)

| Group | Pages |
|---|---|
| Landing | `index.html` |
| Game Modes (7) | `classic`, `cadence-tracker`, `parry-madness`, `elemental-bash`, `shuffle-board`, `quantum-overload`, `battle-for-time` |
| Features (4) | `accessibility`, `customization`, `adjustable-ads`, `charity` |
| Creator | `about-creator` |
| Feedback (2) | `feedback-in-depth`, `feedback-short` |
| Stores (2) | `recommend-store` → `signup-store` |
| Indie Devs (2) | `recommend-indie-dev` → `signup-indie-dev` |
| Testing | `android-tester` |
| Support | `support` |
| Legal | `privacy` |

All pages are plain HTML/CSS with no build step. Shared styling is in `assets/style.css` and shared scripts are in `assets/site.js`.

## Privacy Policy auto-sync

The Privacy Policy page is generated from a Google Doc.

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/sync-privacy.yml` (runs every 6 hours, on manual trigger, and when the script changes)
- Script: `scripts/sync_privacy.py` (Parser → Syntax Converter → Formatter)
- Output: `assets/privacy-content.html` (do not edit by hand, it is overwritten on each sync)

Requirements:
- The Google Doc must be shared as **Anyone with the link: Viewer**.
- Settings → Actions → General → Workflow permissions must be **Read and write**.

To sync immediately: **Actions → Sync Privacy Policy → Run workflow**.

## Forms

The Support, Feedback, Store, Indie Dev and Android Tester pages embed Google Forms using their responder links. To change a form, edit the `FORMS` links in the generated page's `<iframe data-src="...">`.

For forms to work without a Google sign-in, each form must have:
- Collect email addresses: **Do not collect** (or **Responder input**)
- Limit to 1 response: **Off**
- No file upload questions

## Editing

- The landing page is `index.html`.
- Sub pages contain commented section stubs (`<!-- SECTION: ... PURPOSE: ... -->`) with empty `<section>` elements to fill in.
- Screenshots are in `assets/img/`.

If you edit locally, **Pull before you Push**, because the sync bot commits to this repo.
